</style>
<h2>Asobi Review 1.0 (build 2048) <span class="when">Nov 2, 2026</span></h2>
<ul>
<li><b>A cut movie plays straight through</b> in a review, without stopping at each shot.</li>
<li><b>Trimmed clips sound right</b> in reviews streamed from the host.</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<div class="earlier">Earlier updates</div>
<h3>1.0 (build 2039) <span class="when">Nov 2, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Right frame in a live review.</b> On a trimmed clip or a shot of a cut movie, you now see the frame the host is on, and your notes and marks land where you made them.</li>
<li><b>Joining on the right frame.</b> Joining a review in progress takes you to the frame the room is on, with earlier notes and marks in place.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 2031) <span class="when">Nov 1, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Note ticks sit on the right frame</b> on trimmed clips, and loading a new playlist no longer keeps the previous clip's notes on screen.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 2002) <span class="when">Oct 30, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Both ACES looks in the View menu:</b> ACES 1.x and ACES 2.0 views side by side, whichever ACES config is in use.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1998) <span class="when">Oct 30, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li>Small improvements to the guide.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1992) <span class="when">Oct 30, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>A redesigned review window.</b> A title bar above the picture and one docked control bar below it, so nothing sits on the picture. Every control is an icon over its name.</li>
<li><b>One Sidebar</b> beside the picture holds the notes and the playlist; every window opens with the notes showing.</li>
<li><b>A real timeline:</b> each clip is a named block under the picture, with its notes and one playhead.</li>
<li><b>The guide</b> is updated throughout, with new figures.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1966) <span class="when">Oct 29, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li>Small improvements.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0 (build 1963) <span class="when">Oct 29, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li>Small improvements.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
